# migrations.manifest
#
# Byte-identical record of every MIGRATIONS entry (system / main DB) that has
# ever shipped. Format: <version>: <description>  (blank lines and # ignored).
#
# RULES (enforced by migrations_obey_append_only_manifest test):
#   1. Lines below this header are APPEND-ONLY. Never edit, reorder, or remove
#      a line that has already shipped.
#   2. New migration: append (version, description) here AND add the matching
#      Migration entry + dispatch block + const in migrations.rs, same commit.
#   3. To change a published version, append a NEW higher-numbered migration;
#      never edit the old entry (the runner records the version; editing a body
#      silently NO-OPs on existing deployments).
#
# History (2026-05-31, merge upstream aa6a0bec): DOCUMENTED DISCONTINUITY. The
# upstream merge took main version v64 for readd_user_id_memory_core, colliding
# with the VOCSAP v64 (approvals_gate_id, Patch 21). The VOCSAP migration was
# renumbered to v84 (appended after upstream max v83 cred_audit_attribution_columns).
# Its body is idempotent (add_column_if_not_exists) so re-running it under the new
# number is a NO-OP on the single existing deployment (LXC 121, already at v64).
# This manifest was REGENERATED from the merged array; the v64 line now carries
# the upstream description. Only intentional break of byte-identical, tied to merge.

